findings.description:
Line 87 defers "extend existing storage or add a metrology store" to slice design, while calling the data layer the keystone. The choice decides:
- whether samples are per-project files committed to the repo or a user-global store;
- how cross-project joins work;
- how retention interacts with run-state pruning.

Those are architectural. Naming 280 as a candidate also contradicts the plan's "Independent of … 280," and 280 is not started. Given "resist complexity," the architecture should commit to a direction. One option: an append-only user-global store next to `~/.config/squadron/runs/`, holding self-contained snapshots, with no dependency on 280. Slice design would then only settle the format.
